  "body": "Found while gating the #2772 PR (PR #3674) on 2026-11-23. Reproduced on a clean worktree of `origin/main` with no diff, so it is not caused by that PR.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe quick gate's per-crate prebuild machinery wedges deterministically on this machine: cargo 1.99.1's `rmeta` handoff across the gate's per-crate `--no-run` invocations deadlocks, so the prebuild steps never complete. The run hangs until the gate's stall watchdog fires.\n\nThe per-binary fallback works: the touched test binaries run one by one, and clippy runs clean. So the defect is in the prebuild handoff, not the suites.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The per-crate prebuild handoff completes on a clean checkout, or the gate detects the wedge and falls back to the per-binary path with a note.\n- The stall rows name the wedged step.\n\nMachine: Windows, rustc stable (cargo 1.99.1), sccache active. Observed twice: once on the PR worktree, once reproduced on clean `origin/main`.\n",
